    "content": {
     "header": "Architektur",
     "subheader": "",
     "headerLayout": 0,
     "headerPosition": "",
     "headerLink": "",
     "type": "mask_accordions",
     "title": "",
     "text": "",
     "accordion": [
      {
       "uid": "20",
       "title": "Responsibility towards the region",
       "info": "",
       "text": "<p>The cornerstone and starting point for the realisation of eriro was the responsibility towards the region – to create a look with the Alpine hideaway that pays homage to the area’s traditional architecture and the beauty of its historic structures.</p>",
       "linktext": "",
       "link": ""
      },
      {
       "uid": "21",
       "title": "Alpine region aesthetics",
       "info": "",
       "text": "<p>The eriro project seeks to capture the beauty of the simple and traditional. Three typical Alpine saddle roofs – a symbol of the collaboration between the founders – join together in a way that resonates warmth and protection, and open towards the sky at the bend.&nbsp;</p>",
       "linktext": "",
       "link": ""
      },
      {
       "uid": "22",
       "title": "A tribute to the origins ",
       "info": "",
       "text": "<p>The concept of eriro is fuelled by the central tenet of recognising and honouring the importance of origins in all aspects: original Alpine region construction, original knowledge of the properties of plants, such as tanning agents for treating wood, or original need to provide shelter from wind and weather with the right kind of structure.</p>",
       "linktext": "",
       "link": ""
      },
      {
       "uid": "23",
       "title": "Unparalled in time-honoured craftsmanship",
       "info": "",
       "text": "<p>No CNC machines were used for any of the work. The architectural elements are almost exclusively crafted by hand, such as the 4,000 cotter pins, or the long, handcrafted table in the lobby. Each lamp is made by hand. The interior is embellished with woven, bound and carved wood, pure sheep’s wool carpets, and handmade coat hangers by designer huanzn. Even the bathtubs are crafted by hand out of tree trunks and sealed with resin.&nbsp;</p>",
       "linktext": "",
       "link": ""
      },
      {
       "uid": "24",
       "title": "The value of local materials",
       "info": "",
       "text": "<p>In line with the idea of origins, almost all materials are locally sourced. Wood from the surrounding forests is the foundation for all interior materials from floor to ceiling. Architectural detail elements are manufactured and processed in Ehrwald. The roof is shingled with larch from the nearby forests. The wood darkens, a deliberate transformation and finishing that keeps with the Alpine aesthetic.</p>",
       "linktext": "",
       "link": ""
      }
     ]
    }
   },
